 (0 − (-3000)) = -1000 + 3000 = 2000. So the sum is 2000 for A vs. B. If we compute for B vs. A, it would be different. But the reason prefers the lottery with the more favorable sum. So the sum of (a_i − b_j) over all i,j is 2000. This is the only relevant quantity. Therefore, the decision reason is applicable and can be evaluated using the outcomes and probabilities. The information needed is the sum of (outcome of A minus outcome of B) across all outcome pairs, which is 2000. Thus, the decision reason is applicable to this decision problem.",
